ence analysis</article-title><source>Microbiology</source><year>2003</year><volume>149</volume><fpage>217</fpage><lpage>228</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12576595</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="FBN123C18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Everroad</surname><given-names>R. C.</given-names></name><name><surname>Wood</surname><given-names>A. M.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparative molecular evolution of newly discovered picocyanobacterial strains reveals a phylogenetically informative variable region of &#x003b2; phycoerythrin</article-title><source>J. Phycol.</source><year>2006</year><volume>42</volume><fpage>1300</fpage><lpage>1311</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="FBN123C19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Falkowski</surname><given-names>P. G.</given-names></name><name><surname>La Roche</surname><given-names>J.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Acclimation to spectral irradiance in algae</article-title><source>J.Phycol.</source><year>1991</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>8</fpage><lpage>14</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="FBN123C20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Golden</surname><given-names>S. S.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Light-Responsive Gene Expression in Cyanobacteria</article-title><source>J. Bacteriol.</source><year>1995</year><volume>177</volume><fpage>1651</fpage><lpage>1654</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">7896684</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="FBN123C21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Haverkamp</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Acinas</surname><given-names>S. G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Doeleman</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Diversity and phylogeny of Baltic Sea picocyanobacteria inferred from their ITS and phycobiliprotein operons</article-title><source>Environ. Microbiol.</source><year>2008</year><volume>10</volume><fpage>174</fpage><lpage>188</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17903216</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="FBN123C22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Holm-Hansen</surname><given-names>O.</given-names></name><name><surname>Riemann</surname><given-names>B.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Chlorophyll <italic>a</italic> determination: improvements in methodology</article-title><source>Oikos</source><year>1978</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>438</fpage><lpage>447</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="FBN123C23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kana</surname><given-names>T. M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Glibert</surname><given-names>P. M.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effect of irradiances up to 2000 &#x000b5;E m<sup>&#x02212;2</sup> s<sup>&#x02212;1</sup> on marine <italic>Synechococcus</italic> WH7803 &#x02013; I. Growth, pigmentation, and cell composition</article-title><source>Deep-Sea Res.</source><year>1987</year><volume>a 34</volume><fpage>479</fpage><lpage>495</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="FBN123C24"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kana</surname><given-names>T. M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Glibert</surname><given-names>P. M.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effect of irradiances up to 2000 &#x000b5;E m<sup>&#x02212;2</sup> s<sup>&#x02212;1</sup> on marine <italic>Synechococcus</italic> WH7803 &#x02013; II. Photosynthetic responses and mechanisms</article-title><source>Deep-Sea Res.</source><year>1987</year><fpage>b 497</fpage><lpage>516</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="FBN123C25"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kirk</surname><given-names>J. T. O.</given-names></name></person-group><source>Light and Photosynthesis in Aquatic Ecosystems</source><year>1994</year><edition>2nd edn</edition><publisher-loc>Cambridge</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Cambridge University Press</publisher-name></citation></ref><ref id="FBN123C26"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kulkarni</surname><given-names>R. D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Golden</surname><given-names>S. S.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Form II of D1 is important during transition from standard to high light intensity in <italic>Synechococcus</italic> sp. strain PCC7942</article-title><source>Photosynthesis Res.</source><year>1995</year><volume>46</volume><fpage>435</fpage><lpage>443</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="FBN123C27"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>MacIntyre</surname><given-names>H. L.</given-names></name><name><surname>Kana</surname><given-names>T. M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Anning</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Photoacclimation of photosynthesis irradiance response curves and photosynthetic pigments in microalgae and cyanobacteria</article-title><source>J. Phycol.</source><year>2002</year><volume>38</volume><fpage>17</fpage><lpage>38</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="FBN123C28"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Malinsky-Rushansky</surname><given-names>N.</given-names></name><name><surname>Berman</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><name><surname>Berner</surname><given-names>T.</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Physiological characteristics of picophytoplankton, isolated from Lake Kinneret: responses to light and temperature</article-title><source>J. Plankton Res.</source><year>2002</year><volume>24</volume><fpage>1173</fpage><lpage>1183</lpage></c